===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun|~}}

# Soft filling material used in cushions etc.
# {{lb|en|computing}} Extra characters such as spaces added to a record to fill it out to a fixed length.
# {{lb|en|military|cryptography}} Extraneous text added to a message for the purpose of concealing its beginning, ending, or length.<ref name="JP102">Joint Publication 1-02 ''U.S. Department of Defense Dictionary of Military and Associated Terms; 12 April 2001 (As Amended Through 14 April 2006).''</ref>
# Anything of little value used to fill up space.
#: {{ux|en|That magazine is mostly advertisements; the rest is '''padding'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1920|author=Agatha Christie|authorlink=Agatha Christie|title={{w|The Mysterious Affair at Styles}}|publisher=Pan Books|location=London|year_published=1954|page=135|passage=But to my intense surprise, on getting down early the next morning, and eagerly opening the newspapers, there was not a word about the arrest! There was a column of mere '''padding''' about “The Styles Poisoning Case,” but nothing further. It was rather inexplicable, but I supposed that, for some reason or other, Japp wished to keep it out of the papers.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} Robbing on a highway.
# The process of [[mordant]]ing a [[fabric]].

